[2026-09-28T17:52:18.972+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "Renders the registration page reached from the sign-in page through the unique 'Create an account' link and container route /register. Must expose exactly: one textbox with the accessible label 'Username' (type=text, name=username), one textbox labeled 'Email' (type=text, name=email), one password input labeled 'Password', one password input labeled 'Confirm password', one checkbox labeled 'Agree to the terms' that is initially unchecked, and one enabled button named 'Create account'. Password values must never be echoed into visible text, headings, accessible names, or success output. On submit the component calls session.register({ username, email, password, confirmPassword, agreeToTerms }); when the result is not ok it stays on the page, writes every returned error message beside its owning field (grouped error codes -> messages, multiple errors visible simultaneously, plus a confirm-mismatch message beside 'Confirm password'), and preserves the submitted username and email values. The submit button stays enabled and actionable after a failed submit so all messages remain readable. On ok it navigates to /signin (the sign-in form immediately available) without displaying the password. The rendered field messages must come from the server result, not from a frontend-only constant: 'Username already exists', 'Username format is invalid', 'Email format is invalid', 'Password requirements are not satisfied', 'Agree to terms is required'. TODO for TDD: wire useState values to the inputs, implement handleSubmit, render errors with aria-invalid + a message element per field, and extract the field/error rendering if the file approaches 500 lines.",
